WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:03.200
-Seth Meyers.
-It's so nice to be back.

00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:04.801
-Yeah. You're looking sharp.
-Thank you, man.

00:00:04.801 --> 00:00:05.834
-Looking good.
-Thank you.

00:00:05.834 --> 00:00:08.634
-Do you miss me?

00:00:08.634 --> 00:00:10.033
Seeing and talking to me
every day.

00:00:10.033 --> 00:00:11.601
-I do.

00:00:11.601 --> 00:00:14.868
We weirdly -- We overlapped
for two years on "SNL."

00:00:14.868 --> 00:00:18.501
We weirdly spent more time
collaborating on this podcast.

00:00:18.501 --> 00:00:19.534
It was the best.

00:00:19.534 --> 00:00:21.367
-I had
such a great time doing it.

00:00:21.367 --> 00:00:23.100
I mean, I know you
and I'm friends with you,

00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:24.334
but really got to know you.

00:00:24.334 --> 00:00:27.300
And we spent like 15 hours
together talking.

00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:29.267
-It was, yeah,
I think the very fact

00:00:29.267 --> 00:00:32.334
that we had to make this podcast

00:00:32.334 --> 00:00:35.200
and it forced us all
to talk about ourselves,

00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:36.367
it was a very cool thing

00:00:36.367 --> 00:00:38.133
and I felt very lucky
to do it with you.

00:00:38.133 --> 00:00:39.968
-Yeah, I agree.
Thank you, buddy.

00:00:39.968 --> 00:00:41.667
It was us. It was me and you.

00:00:41.667 --> 00:00:43.067
It was Jimmy Kimmel.
-It's not important.

00:00:43.067 --> 00:00:44.234
It's not important who
the other people were.

00:00:44.234 --> 00:00:45.767
[ Laughter ]
-That's right. Doesn't matter.

00:00:45.767 --> 00:00:48.667
-It's you, me, and three guys.
It doesn't matter who they are.

00:00:48.667 --> 00:00:50.467
-Yeah.
-Could be three nobodies.

00:00:50.467 --> 00:00:53.267
It basically was.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:53.267 --> 00:00:54.901
-We kind of got to know
what we were doing, though,

00:00:54.901 --> 00:00:57.767
by the end.
-Yeah, but you were the best.

00:00:57.767 --> 00:00:59.434
-No.
-Yeah. No, everybody --

00:00:59.434 --> 00:01:01.501
Look, you hosted
the fifth episode.

00:01:01.501 --> 00:01:03.567
-We all had to host an episode.
-Yes.

00:01:03.567 --> 00:01:05.200
And so you hosted
"The Newlywed Game."

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:07.133
We were foolish enough.

00:01:07.133 --> 00:01:09.300
We gave Jimmy all of
our wives' phone numbers.

00:01:09.300 --> 00:01:10.901
-Yeah.
-Which never do.

00:01:10.901 --> 00:01:12.968
If a dude's like, "Hey, I want
all your wives' numbers,"

00:01:12.968 --> 00:01:14.434
we're like, "Hey, okay."

00:01:14.434 --> 00:01:17.434
You'd be better off giving away
your Social Security number.

00:01:17.434 --> 00:01:18.901
-I have everyone's wives'
numbers.

00:01:18.901 --> 00:01:20.000
I thought it was interesting

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:21.667
because we're
all talk show hosts

00:01:21.667 --> 00:01:25.100
and we're all luckily
very happily married man.

00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:27.300
And we have families. I go,
"That could be a fun episode.

00:01:27.300 --> 00:01:28.701
Let's talk to the wives
who actually see

00:01:28.701 --> 00:01:32.901
how crazy we really are
and see how our answers match."

00:01:32.901 --> 00:01:34.300
-Yeah, like
a "Newlywed Game" style.

00:01:34.300 --> 00:01:36.934
It should have worked.
-Yes, it should have been that.

00:01:36.934 --> 00:01:38.234
-Yeah, but it was --

00:01:38.234 --> 00:01:40.100
It ended up
being something better.

00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:41.734
-Dude, John Oliver
is laughing so hard.

00:01:41.734 --> 00:01:43.167
I think he, like,
broke a rib or something.

00:01:43.167 --> 00:01:45.801
-It was -- John Oliver --
you know, of all of us

00:01:45.801 --> 00:01:48.067
maybe the most capable
of stoicism --

00:01:48.067 --> 00:01:50.234
laughed so hard at the way
you phrased the questions

00:01:50.234 --> 00:01:52.167
that he kept falling
out of the Zoom box.

00:01:52.167 --> 00:01:54.734
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah, he was falling down.

00:01:54.734 --> 00:01:57.868
-He would come back through
like a pendulum.

00:01:57.868 --> 00:01:59.901
-Well, you know what?

00:01:59.901 --> 00:02:01.400
What happened was because
I was like, alright,

00:02:01.400 --> 00:02:03.400
I don't want to bother
the wives, you know,

00:02:03.400 --> 00:02:05.434
but I wanted to ask them
the questions like,

00:02:05.434 --> 00:02:07.567
"When did you first fall
in love" or whatever.

00:02:07.567 --> 00:02:09.934
So I just wrote them in a text

00:02:09.934 --> 00:02:13.634
and I just sent them texts
with not even really questions.

00:02:13.634 --> 00:02:16.767
-You used a lot
of pronouns loosely.

00:02:16.767 --> 00:02:18.868
-So didn't know if you were
talking about you or them.

00:02:18.868 --> 00:02:21.667
-Yeah, the best one
in the first episode you --

00:02:21.667 --> 00:02:25.667
because you just wrote to my
wife, "Pet name" question mark.

00:02:25.667 --> 00:02:28.133
And now I think that my wife
should have assumed

00:02:28.133 --> 00:02:30.167
you meant what pet names
we have for each other.

00:02:30.167 --> 00:02:32.000
-So you were like, "I know what
it is. It's 'babe.'"

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:33.968
-Yeah. I thought our pet name
for each other is "babe."

00:02:33.968 --> 00:02:36.133
I explained it to -- Long story.

00:02:36.133 --> 00:02:40.267
-And I said, "I think your wife
misunderstood the question"

00:02:40.267 --> 00:02:42.834
because I think she gave us
your actual pet name.

00:02:42.834 --> 00:02:44.067
Your pet's name.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:44.067 --> 00:02:46.567
-She texted Jimmy Frisbee,
which is our pet's name.

00:02:46.567 --> 00:02:48.167
[ Laughter ]

00:02:48.167 --> 00:02:50.567
And the funny part about that

00:02:50.567 --> 00:02:53.634
is that would be the dumbest
question on "The Newlywed Game."

00:02:53.634 --> 00:02:56.667
Like, imagine if you couldn't
match with your spouse

00:02:56.667 --> 00:02:59.234
what the name of your pet is.
-Yeah, exactly.

00:02:59.234 --> 00:03:00.968
-Like, that's not even like
you don't know each other.

00:03:00.968 --> 00:03:02.167
You might not live together.

00:03:02.167 --> 00:03:03.734
[ Laughter ]

00:03:03.734 --> 00:03:05.167
-Yeah, I think Colbert was like,

00:03:05.167 --> 00:03:07.400
"This is turning into like
an Alzheimer's exam."

00:03:07.400 --> 00:03:09.234
Like, who's the president?
-Who is? Yeah.

00:03:09.234 --> 00:03:10.801
-What year is it?
-Yeah.

00:03:10.801 --> 00:03:12.567
And then we went back
to the well,

00:03:12.567 --> 00:03:14.234
which is a very dangerous
thing to do in comedy

00:03:14.234 --> 00:03:16.133
because you had a lot
of questions you'd ask them

00:03:16.133 --> 00:03:17.701
that we hadn't gotten to
in episode 5.

00:03:17.701 --> 00:03:20.400
In episode 11, we did it again
and it was equally good

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:22.667
because you weren't allowed
to go back

00:03:22.667 --> 00:03:24.167
and ask the questions better

00:03:24.167 --> 00:03:26.100
because you had to use
the original answer.

00:03:26.100 --> 00:03:28.901
-Yeah, the original bad answers
from the original question.

00:03:28.901 --> 00:03:30.834
-Yeah.
-Questionnaire that I sent out.

00:03:30.834 --> 00:03:32.968
-Also, my wife was --
let's be honest --

00:03:32.968 --> 00:03:36.501
my wife took this
as an opportunity to do bits.

00:03:36.501 --> 00:03:40.267
-What we devised from
interviewing your wife

00:03:40.267 --> 00:03:41.834
is that she's trying
to kill you.

00:03:41.834 --> 00:03:44.200
-Yeah, like, it was like,
"What's the hardest

00:03:44.200 --> 00:03:45.667
you've laughed," And I'm like,
"Oh, that's funny.

00:03:45.667 --> 00:03:47.100
Our kids said
this funny thing."

00:03:47.100 --> 00:03:49.400
And then her answer was "the
time he fell out of a canoe."

00:03:49.400 --> 00:03:51.734
[ Laughter ]

00:03:51.734 --> 00:03:54.767
They were all like -- it was
like evil had befallen me.

00:03:54.767 --> 00:03:57.234
And then she copped
to another answer

00:03:57.234 --> 00:03:58.434
she gave you that
we didn't get to

00:03:58.434 --> 00:03:59.667
that I think proves my point

00:03:59.667 --> 00:04:02.968
that I'm about
to be knocked off.

00:04:02.968 --> 00:04:05.434
-I sent a bunch of --
I sent a speed round.

00:04:05.434 --> 00:04:06.934
We didn't get to all of these.

00:04:06.934 --> 00:04:10.734
So I'm like, "Salty or sweet?"
Again, I didn't say who.

00:04:10.734 --> 00:04:12.634
-Yeah.
-I didn't say the husbands

00:04:12.634 --> 00:04:13.767
or the wives.
-Yeah.

00:04:13.767 --> 00:04:15.567
-So people were
answering for themselves.

00:04:15.567 --> 00:04:17.234
-Or the husband
or you never even knew.

00:04:17.234 --> 00:04:18.501
Right.
-I, to this day,

00:04:18.501 --> 00:04:20.267
don't know
what question I asked.

00:04:20.267 --> 00:04:22.834
I don't know why I expected it.
But she said salty.

00:04:22.834 --> 00:04:26.701
I think she meant her?
-I think she is a salty person.

00:04:26.701 --> 00:04:27.968
Yeah.
-No, no, no, that's not what --

00:04:27.968 --> 00:04:30.834
-Based on her answers, Jimmy.
-No. Okay, listen.

00:04:30.834 --> 00:04:34.501
Morning person, then where
you proposed.

00:04:34.501 --> 00:04:37.334
The fifth one I asked, I said,
"Big spoon or little spoon?"

00:04:37.334 --> 00:04:38.934
-Yeah.
-I just thought
it'd be funny because --

00:04:38.934 --> 00:04:41.567
-That's a good question.
-I think that'd be hilarious.

00:04:41.567 --> 00:04:44.234
-My wife's answer
is not a funny answer.

00:04:44.234 --> 00:04:45.734
Look what she wrote.

00:04:45.734 --> 00:04:46.767
Knife.

00:04:46.767 --> 00:04:50.834
[ Laughter ]

00:04:50.834 --> 00:04:54.901
When I go missing, Jimmy,
go to that.

00:04:54.901 --> 00:04:57.467
Send the police to my apartment.

00:04:57.467 --> 00:05:00.400
-It was really funny.
Alexi, that was great.

00:05:00.400 --> 00:05:03.367
-This is very good. Very salty.
-Very, very funny.

00:05:03.367 --> 00:05:04.501
She was fan-- All the --
-She did.

00:05:04.501 --> 00:05:05.868
I think she did a very good job.

00:05:05.868 --> 00:05:08.033
I'm actually very proud of her
for her comedy choices.

00:05:08.033 --> 00:05:10.067
-All the wives
were extremely funny.

00:05:10.067 --> 00:05:12.934
And I go, "Wow, we're so lucky,
for God's sakes."

00:05:12.934 --> 00:05:15.834
-Those were her --
The ones where she, the focus

00:05:15.834 --> 00:05:17.200
was on her were
her two favorites,

00:05:17.200 --> 00:05:18.434
and she didn't listen
to the other 10.

00:05:18.434 --> 00:05:20.701
-[ Laughs ] I love her.
You know what?

00:05:20.701 --> 00:05:22.400
I loved her because she popped
in one of the Zooms

00:05:22.400 --> 00:05:23.501
wearing a
"Late Night with Jimmy" --

00:05:23.501 --> 00:05:24.834
-That was also very hurtful.

00:05:24.834 --> 00:05:27.634
We're doing a Zoom
and she has a "Late Night,"

00:05:27.634 --> 00:05:30.000
not even a "Tonight Show,"
"A Late Night with Jimmy Fallon"

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:33.234
T-shirt from
when he had my show.

00:05:33.234 --> 00:05:35.968
-I didn't have your show.
I had my show.

00:05:35.968 --> 00:05:37.334
-Look, she's my wife!

00:05:37.334 --> 00:05:38.534
[ Laughter ]

00:05:38.534 --> 00:05:41.033
-I have her cellphone number.

00:05:41.033 --> 00:05:42.734
-She came in wearing --

00:05:42.734 --> 00:05:44.868
She showed it
to all the other hosts.

00:05:44.868 --> 00:05:46.868
"Here I am
in my Jimmy shirt."

00:05:46.868 --> 00:05:50.033
-Yeah. And then we started
talking about merch.

00:05:50.033 --> 00:05:51.534
-Oh, yeah.
-In the NBC store.

00:05:51.534 --> 00:05:53.167
-Yeah, this is --
Look, I brought proof

00:05:53.167 --> 00:05:54.834
because I feel like --
I don't want to come off

00:05:54.834 --> 00:05:57.033
